# CKB AI Bench - environment overrides (copy to .env for local use; .env is gitignored).
#
# Every key below is read by ckbbench/config.py (the single source of truth). Service defaults are
# usable without a .env; a paid model still needs its provider credential. Set a key only to
# retarget a run without editing code. Parenthesized legacy names apply only where explicitly shown;
# selected model profiles deliberately read only CKBBENCH_LLM_API_KEY.
#
# These are NOT secrets. DevNet genesis keys are public dev.toml test keys (ADR-0007).

# --- LLM provider (OpenAI-compatible Responses API) ---
# CKBBENCH_LLM_API_KEY=sk-noauth
#   The selected profile supplies the endpoint, model, protocol settings and bounded request-body
#   extensions. The credential stays in .env and never enters a profile, result, log or diagnostic.
# CKBBENCH_LLM_API_BASE=http://localhost:18321/v1      # (BENCH_API_BASE)
#   Development-only fallback for unprofiled dry runs. A scored run always uses its profile base.

# --- MCP server under test (version pinned + preflight-enforced, ADR-0010) ---
# CKBBENCH_MCP_URL=https://mcp.ckbdev.com/ckbai          # (MCP_URL) live dev default
# CKBBENCH_MCP_VERSION=1.6.13                            # (MCP_PINNED_VERSION)

# --- Chain RPC endpoints (DevNet + TestNet scored separately) ---
# Defaults are addresses as seen FROM THE HARNESS HOST. Inside the docker network the
# orchestrator overrides DEVNET_RPC with the sidecar's compose service name.
# CKBBENCH_DEVNET_RPC=http://127.0.0.1:8114
# CKBBENCH_TESTNET_RPC=https://testnet.ckb.dev/rpc

# --- Container images (pin at release; supports repo:tag or repo@sha256:...) ---
# CKBBENCH_AGENT_IMAGE=ckbbench-agent:latest
# CKBBENCH_VERIFIER_IMAGE=ckbbench-verifier:latest

# --- Run cleanup (default: delete ephemeral docker/host resources after each cell) ---
# CKBBENCH_KEEP=0            # 1 / true keeps agent containers, work+cargo volumes, host run dirs
# CKBBENCH_DOCKER=0          # 1 wires docker runner + proxy violation check

# --- Legacy matrix TestNet signing (operator secret; gitignored via .env) ---
# Funded sender private key for task-04-send-tx. Either name works; only the ones you export are
# forwarded to a legacy matrix TestNet cell. A live key never reaches a DevNet cell.
# CKBBENCH_TESTNET_SENDER_PRIVKEY=0x...                 # (BENCH_TESTNET_SENDER_PRIVKEY)

# Independent campaigns use an owner-private signer-pool file supplied with --signer-pool, not
# this environment variable. See docs/SIGNER_POOL.md for its schema, validation and funding flow.

# --- Agent-visible chain context (set by the harness per cell; NOT operator settings) ---
# The harness sets these for the cell's chain, identically in every arm. They are listed so an
# operator can recognize them, not so they can be overridden: an exported host value is
# deliberately outranked by the cell's own values, and the signer names a cell must not carry are
# blanked in local mode.
#   CKBBENCH_CHAIN_PROFILE   every cell: devnet | testnet
#   CKB_RPC_URL              every cell: endpoint reachable from the agent's namespace (docker
#                            service name for DevNet; the configured URL, complete, otherwise)
#   CKB_SENDER_PRIVKEY       Legacy DevNet matrix cells only: the PUBLIC dev.toml genesis fixture from
#                            ckbbench/config.py. Published material -- never fund it and never
#                            reuse it on TestNet or Mainnet. Independent campaigns expose only
#                            the constrained signer broker described in docs/SIGNER_POOL.md.
#   CKB_SDK_HOME             docker cells only (it is an agent-image contract): the path holding
#                            the pinned offline @ckb-ccc/core install. Local runs have no SDK path.
